                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h2]Like Episode 1 but the short story continues[/h2]\r\n\r\nI played through Jacob Jones Episodes 1 and 2 last year and it was actually quite fun to play although it is way too short. Too bad they didn't make any more episodes.\r\n\r\nThe Jacob Jones games are similar to the older Professor Layton series. It contains some brain teasers and I didn't find them too challenging.\r\n\r\nThe art design is cute and still holds up well today. Cartoonish graphics never get old to me. The voice acting is well done and the story is simple.\r\n\r\nThe collection achievements, just like in the first episode, are for the most part straightforward and easy to obtain. This time around I had some trouble finding all of the soda cans, even with the help of a guide lol. Some of the soda cans were also hard to pick up. I had to move the camera to the right spot to be able to click them, a bit buggy.\r\n\r\nMy inner child very much enjoyed playing the Jacob Jones episodes. I recommend both episodes if you're looking for short games to 100 percent.\r\n\r\n[h2]7/10[/h2]\r\n\r\n[h3][url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/45905648-Gork%2527s-Game-Grind/]Check out my curated list of games[/url][/h3]",
